1
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:33,480
[Weechana]

2
00:01:41,537 --> 00:01:43,338
<i>Eva.</i>

3
00:01:44,076 --> 00:01:47,620
<i>I'm so sorry about Domino.</i>

4
00:01:47,620 --> 00:01:49,529
<i>I really am.</i>

5
00:01:49,529 --> 00:01:52,494
<i>But I swear, I had nothing to do with this.</i>

6
00:01:54,350 --> 00:01:57,434
<i>And it breaks my heart that you think I did.</i>

7
00:01:59,494 --> 00:02:04,254
<i>I don't know what made you think
I'd do something like that.</i>

8
00:02:07,534 --> 00:02:10,043
<i>Seeing what you're going through,</i>

9
00:02:10,043 --> 00:02:15,654
<i>I've decided not to ask you to help
with my campaign anymore.</i>

10
00:02:16,820 --> 00:02:19,006
<i>But if you ever need anything,</i>

11
00:02:19,006 --> 00:02:21,641
<i>I'm still here for you, just like always.</i>

12
00:02:21,641 --> 00:02:23,998
<i>And when the campaign is over,</i>

13
00:02:23,998 --> 00:02:27,099
<i>I hope we can talk things through.</i>

14
00:02:27,801 --> 00:02:29,602
<i>I love you.</i>

15
00:02:40,041 --> 00:02:42,094
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to overhear.

16
00:02:42,094 --> 00:02:44,774
I was just going downstairs
to get some water.

17
00:02:45,604 --> 00:02:48,646
Oh, I see.

18
00:02:48,646 --> 00:02:49,932
This way.

19
00:02:49,932 --> 00:02:51,384
Okay.

20
00:03:04,694 --> 00:03:06,290
What do you think?

21
00:03:06,290 --> 00:03:07,921
Huh?

22
00:03:07,921 --> 00:03:09,391
About what?

23
00:03:10,713 --> 00:03:15,129
Weechana said he'd leave me alone
for a while.

24
00:03:16,852 --> 00:03:20,385
Well... he probably meant it.

25
00:03:20,385 --> 00:03:24,534
He had his campaign to focus on,
and you were grieving.

26
00:03:24,534 --> 00:03:26,654
I think he did the right thing.

27
00:03:33,561 --> 00:03:35,374
Do you think...

28
00:03:36,532 --> 00:03:38,734
I'll be able to break up with him?

29
00:03:39,694 --> 00:03:41,495
Do you want to?

30
00:03:43,764 --> 00:03:46,694
Everything was fine at first.

31
00:03:47,505 --> 00:03:50,228
But lately... I don't know.

32
00:03:50,228 --> 00:03:52,174
Something just hasn't felt right.

33
00:03:52,844 --> 00:03:54,734
Not just with Weechana,

34
00:03:55,718 --> 00:03:57,534
but with his family too.

35
00:04:01,545 --> 00:04:04,574
If you were my friend,

36
00:04:07,774 --> 00:04:09,814
would you tell me to let him go?

37
00:04:11,212 --> 00:04:12,738
Well...

38
00:04:13,713 --> 00:04:15,729
If I were your friend,

39
00:04:15,729 --> 00:04:19,809
I'd tell you to think it through carefully.

40
00:04:19,809 --> 00:04:22,054
I don't think love...

41
00:04:23,129 --> 00:04:25,214
is supposed to hurt anyone.

42
00:04:27,034 --> 00:04:31,314
I don't want my friend living in danger
or getting hurt.

43
00:04:34,252 --> 00:04:36,294
You've been crying too much...

44
00:04:37,633 --> 00:04:39,834
and you've been forcing yourself
to smile all the time.

45
00:04:42,214 --> 00:04:44,374
And if you were speaking to me
not as a friend,

46
00:04:46,078 --> 00:04:48,534
but as a man,

47
00:04:50,046 --> 00:04:52,254
what would you say?

48
00:04:54,617 --> 00:04:56,614
I'd tell you that...

49
00:04:58,270 --> 00:05:01,374
I believe you deserve someone
who can love you better.

50
00:05:14,771 --> 00:05:16,996
Goodnight.

51
00:05:16,996 --> 00:05:18,797
Goodnight.

52
00:05:42,508 --> 00:05:44,309
This way, please.

53
00:05:46,566 --> 00:05:49,441
Don't worry. This is my friend's restaurant.

54
00:05:49,441 --> 00:05:52,694
No one knows we're meeting here.

55
00:05:52,694 --> 00:05:54,532
Please, have a seat.

56
00:05:54,532 --> 00:05:56,333
Thank you.

57
00:05:58,428 --> 00:06:02,174
I'm sorry about your friend.

58
00:06:03,206 --> 00:06:05,007
Thanks.

59
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:14,479
This is a video Domino secretly recorded
at the party

60
00:06:14,479 --> 00:06:16,300
the night before
the reporter's body was found.

61
00:06:16,300 --> 00:06:18,454
<i>The footage isn't very clear, though.</i>

62
00:06:18,454 --> 00:06:20,462
And this one is...

63
00:06:20,462 --> 00:06:24,063
a video Domino secretly recorded
outside my private gym

64
00:06:24,063 --> 00:06:26,201
the day Weechana came and caused a scene.

65
00:06:26,201 --> 00:06:28,902
That's why I think she was killed
to keep her quiet.

66
00:06:30,612 --> 00:06:34,622
This video could hurt Weechana's reputation
and the party's image.

67
00:06:34,622 --> 00:06:38,468
But from a legal standpoint,

68
00:06:38,468 --> 00:06:40,614
I have to be honest,

69
00:06:41,742 --> 00:06:43,534
it isn't enough for us
to take any action yet.

70
00:06:43,534 --> 00:06:44,974
But we can use it as evidence.

71
00:06:44,974 --> 00:06:47,060
I'm not saying it's completely useless.

72
00:06:47,060 --> 00:06:50,836
Let's look at each piece of evidence
separately.

73
00:06:50,836 --> 00:06:52,654
The video of him causing a scene

74
00:06:52,654 --> 00:06:57,300
could be used to petition the court
for a restraining order.

75
00:06:57,300 --> 00:06:58,729
That's definitely an option.

76
00:06:58,729 --> 00:07:00,181
But to be honest,

77
00:07:01,134 --> 00:07:04,916
those orders usually work on ordinary people.

78
00:07:04,916 --> 00:07:07,524
I doubt they'd have much effect
on someone as powerful as him.

79
00:07:07,524 --> 00:07:10,484
What about the video
that shows him assaulting the reporter?

80
00:07:10,484 --> 00:07:12,561
From what I can see,

81
00:07:12,561 --> 00:07:14,956
the video isn't clear enough
to positively identify the person.

82
00:07:14,956 --> 00:07:16,757
It would most likely be thrown out.

83
00:07:17,998 --> 00:07:21,534
Then if it's useless, why was she still...

84
00:07:24,726 --> 00:07:27,014
Because she was an eyewitness.

85
00:07:28,257 --> 00:07:30,094
And so are you.

86
00:07:32,054 --> 00:07:36,254
So you're saying...
there's nothing we can do?

87
00:07:37,041 --> 00:07:39,345
For now, the best we can do

88
00:07:39,345 --> 00:07:41,662
is file a police report
together with the autopsy findings.

89
00:07:41,662 --> 00:07:43,452
Based on everything you've told me,

90
00:07:43,452 --> 00:07:45,041
there do seem to be suspicious circumstances.

91
00:07:45,041 --> 00:07:47,206
We have sufficient grounds
to proceed with the investigation.

92
00:07:47,206 --> 00:07:51,414
You did the right thing
by requesting an autopsy, Pun.

93
00:07:55,125 --> 00:08:00,374
Eva, do you have her phone and computer?

94
00:08:02,137 --> 00:08:04,649
I haven't been back home yet.

95
00:08:04,649 --> 00:08:08,948
But I don't think there'd be
any evidence left by now.

96
00:08:09,588 --> 00:08:11,065
I think so.

97
00:08:11,065 --> 00:08:13,234
I don't think the criminal
would have left them behind.

98
00:08:15,878 --> 00:08:18,779
Do you happen to know
her Apple ID and password?

99
00:08:22,070 --> 00:08:24,753
I think... she gave it to me.

100
00:08:24,753 --> 00:08:26,865
Can I use your phone?

101
00:08:26,865 --> 00:08:28,358
If you have it, let's access her account.

102
00:08:28,358 --> 00:08:31,614
There might be something in there
that we don't have yet.

103
00:08:36,486 --> 00:08:38,838
There's nothing in here.

104
00:08:38,838 --> 00:08:41,452
What about the voice recording?

105
00:08:41,452 --> 00:08:43,253
I found something.

106
00:08:44,838 --> 00:08:47,054
The latest recording was made...

107
00:08:47,884 --> 00:08:49,894
on the day she died.

108
00:08:50,908 --> 00:08:53,142
<i>Grandma Jit told you
to break into Eva's place,</i>

109
00:08:53,142 --> 00:08:55,996
<i>and you showed up with a man
who looked like he was going to attack me.</i>

110
00:08:55,996 --> 00:08:57,797
<i>What is your plan?</i>

111
00:08:58,524 --> 00:09:00,966
<i>What are you doing?</i>

112
00:09:03,271 --> 00:09:05,430
<i>Why did you bring a knife?</i>

113
00:09:05,430 --> 00:09:09,078
<i>I saw Weechana beat up the reporter,</i>

114
00:09:09,078 --> 00:09:10,879
<i>who later died.</i>

115
00:09:11,569 --> 00:09:14,550
<i>Eva didn't see any of it.
She was in the restroom.</i>

116
00:09:14,550 --> 00:09:17,062
<i>I couldn't bring myself to tell her.</i>

117
00:09:17,062 --> 00:09:20,294
<i>He was her boyfriend, after all.</i>

118
00:09:21,190 --> 00:09:24,105
<i>Ms. Jit would like you to work for her.</i>

119
00:09:24,105 --> 00:09:26,462
<i>What is your rate?</i>

120
00:09:26,462 --> 00:09:28,212
<i>Work?</i>

121
00:09:28,212 --> 00:09:29,598
<i>What do you mean?</i>

122
00:09:29,598 --> 00:09:32,492
<i>Report everything about Eva to her.</i>

123
00:09:32,492 --> 00:09:35,692
<i>Everything on Eva's schedule
has to go through her as well.</i>

124
00:09:35,692 --> 00:09:37,214
<i>500,000.</i>

125
00:09:37,990 --> 00:09:41,142
<i>I get paid really well working for Eva.</i>

126
00:09:41,142 --> 00:09:43,148
<i>No problem.</i>

127
00:09:43,148 --> 00:09:45,420
<i>I'll need the iCloud password.</i>

128
00:09:45,420 --> 00:09:48,225
<i>I want to check what's in the account.</i>

129
00:09:48,225 --> 00:09:51,086
<i>You are deleting the videos
of Weechana assaulting people.</i>

130
00:09:51,086 --> 00:09:52,887
<i>Why are you deleting them?</i>

131
00:09:57,526 --> 00:09:59,574
<i>Give it to me!</i>

132
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:01,972
<i>Stop!</i>

133
00:10:06,558 --> 00:10:09,732
This should be enough
to start building a case against him, right?

134
00:10:09,732 --> 00:10:11,534
Yes.

135
00:10:11,534 --> 00:10:14,974
But it has to be handled by officers
who can't be interfered with.

136
00:10:14,974 --> 00:10:18,054
Well, that's you, isn't it?

137
00:10:19,956 --> 00:10:23,654
I've been pulled off every case
involving the Chaichana family.

138
00:10:25,313 --> 00:10:27,980
A police general stepped in
and took over himself.

139
00:10:27,980 --> 00:10:30,796
His name is Police General Noppol.

140
00:10:30,796 --> 00:10:33,126
Is he one of Weechana's people?

141
00:10:33,126 --> 00:10:35,089
He's been friends with his father
since they were in high school.

142
00:10:35,089 --> 00:10:36,849
They're still very close,

143
00:10:36,849 --> 00:10:38,854
and he's known Weechana since he was a child.

144
00:10:42,364 --> 00:10:44,054
Eva, could we ask you a few questions?

145
00:10:44,054 --> 00:10:49,014
Do you know what might have
motivated Domino to take her own life?

146
00:10:50,609 --> 00:10:53,889
<i>These are exclusive images of Eva
returning to her residence</i>

147
00:10:53,889 --> 00:10:57,841
<i>after attending the funeral
of her longtime manager, Domino.</i>

148
00:10:57,841 --> 00:11:00,396
<i>She declined to comment
on any questions from the media,</i>

149
00:11:00,396 --> 00:11:02,434
<i>including reports suggesting that Domino</i>

150
00:11:02,434 --> 00:11:04,793
<i>had been struggling
with substantial illegal debts</i>

151
00:11:04,793 --> 00:11:06,457
<i>and was suffering from depression,</i>

152
00:11:06,457 --> 00:11:09,310
<i>which are believed to have led her
to take her own life</i>

153
00:11:09,310 --> 00:11:12,174
<i>at Eva's condominium.</i>

154
00:11:57,950 --> 00:11:59,934
Do you think this is okay?

155
00:12:02,148 --> 00:12:03,550
Yeah.

156
00:12:03,550 --> 00:12:06,084
Maybe we should keep the brand shoots
to a minimum for now.

157
00:12:06,084 --> 00:12:08,542
Keep it light,
I don't want her to overwork herself.

158
00:12:08,542 --> 00:12:10,454
So... what about your workouts?

159
00:12:10,454 --> 00:12:12,249
What are you gonna do?

160
00:12:12,249 --> 00:12:16,631
If she still wants the role,
I think she needs to get back to training.

161
00:12:16,631 --> 00:12:18,432
She also needs to keep up
with her English lessons.

162
00:12:19,388 --> 00:12:22,721
Yeah, I've been thinking about that too.

163
00:12:22,721 --> 00:12:24,634
For now, watching her diet is helping,

164
00:12:24,634 --> 00:12:27,134
but if this goes on much longer,
she's gonna start losing muscle.

165
00:12:27,905 --> 00:12:31,158
I'll talk to her tomorrow
and see what she wants to do.

166
00:12:31,158 --> 00:12:33,534
I want her to do what she truly wants.

167
00:12:36,406 --> 00:12:38,574
What? What's the matter?

168
00:12:40,740 --> 00:12:42,654
Sure, it sounds good to me.

169
00:12:43,854 --> 00:12:46,724
Alright, let's call it a night.

170
00:12:46,724 --> 00:12:48,126
I'm getting tired.

171
00:12:48,126 --> 00:12:49,806
It's my bedtime.

172
00:12:49,806 --> 00:12:52,681
Yeah, go get some sleep.

173
00:12:52,681 --> 00:12:54,244
I'm almost finished here.

174
00:12:54,244 --> 00:12:57,070
Get some sleep. You need to stay handsome.

175
00:12:57,070 --> 00:12:58,649
You know it, man.

176
00:12:58,649 --> 00:13:00,868
I need my beauty rest.

177
00:13:00,868 --> 00:13:03,788
- Beauty rest?
- Yeah, I'm heading to bed now.

178
00:13:03,788 --> 00:13:05,934
- Goodnight.
- Goodnight.

179
00:13:24,310 --> 00:13:27,265
What? I thought you needed your beauty sleep.

180
00:13:27,265 --> 00:13:29,134
I'm already beautiful.

181
00:13:33,260 --> 00:13:35,061
You couldn't sleep, could you?

182
00:13:37,665 --> 00:13:39,574
Damn.

183
00:13:39,574 --> 00:13:41,590
How does Pun always have such perfect timing?

184
00:13:41,590 --> 00:13:43,665
He stayed up all night
doing all this for her,

185
00:13:43,665 --> 00:13:45,692
and she just happened to catch him.

186
00:13:45,692 --> 00:13:49,520
I bailed and went to bed early,
so now I look like the jerk.

187
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:52,098
Gosh, gosh, gosh...

188
00:13:53,310 --> 00:13:56,654
Pun, I'll let you have this one.

189
00:14:01,972 --> 00:14:03,692
Hey.

190
00:14:03,692 --> 00:14:06,705
You really didn't have to do all this for me.

191
00:14:06,705 --> 00:14:08,534
It's not your job.

192
00:14:09,830 --> 00:14:11,606
I just...

193
00:14:11,606 --> 00:14:14,734
can't bring myself to accept someone
taking her place yet.

194
00:14:18,441 --> 00:14:21,070
Oh, it's nothing.

195
00:14:21,070 --> 00:14:23,380
I don't mind at all.

196
00:14:23,380 --> 00:14:27,172
It's a little confusing, but I'll be okay.

197
00:14:27,172 --> 00:14:30,068
Boat and I will handle everything for you

198
00:14:30,068 --> 00:14:32,158
until you're feeling better.

199
00:14:32,158 --> 00:14:33,684
All for free.

200
00:14:33,684 --> 00:14:36,614
Absolutely no charge.

201
00:14:43,542 --> 00:14:48,335
I don't want people to remember Domino
as someone who was buried in debt

202
00:14:49,814 --> 00:14:52,534
and driven to suicide by depression.

203
00:14:53,910 --> 00:14:58,494
I'll do whatever it takes
to make sure everyone knows the truth.

204
00:15:02,581 --> 00:15:04,382
I know.

205
00:15:06,076 --> 00:15:07,877
I get it.

206
00:15:08,638 --> 00:15:12,694
And I believe the truth
will come to light one day.

207
00:15:16,553 --> 00:15:18,374
Can I say something?

208
00:15:19,433 --> 00:15:20,925
Sure.

209
00:15:24,078 --> 00:15:28,974
I know you're overwhelmed
and grieving right now.

210
00:15:30,304 --> 00:15:34,054
But you can't give up on your dream.

211
00:15:35,060 --> 00:15:36,934
It still matters.

212
00:15:38,774 --> 00:15:41,854
Lately, you can barely focus
on your film at all.

213
00:15:50,580 --> 00:15:54,094
I know. But what can I do?

214
00:15:55,268 --> 00:15:57,034
I'm in the news every single day.

215
00:15:57,034 --> 00:16:01,374
And every story that comes out is bad.

216
00:16:02,956 --> 00:16:06,254
I don't even know if they still want me
in the film anymore.

217
00:16:08,390 --> 00:16:10,191
Then face it.

218
00:16:11,308 --> 00:16:15,174
Walk right up to them and tell them straight.

219
00:16:16,486 --> 00:16:18,287
You deserve to know.

220
00:16:20,172 --> 00:16:22,374
And they deserve to make their choice.

221
00:16:25,190 --> 00:16:27,889
Hey, listen.

222
00:16:27,889 --> 00:16:30,234
When life gets complicated,

223
00:16:31,174 --> 00:16:33,676
you just gotta break things down,

224
00:16:33,676 --> 00:16:36,054
deal with one problem at a time.

225
00:16:37,974 --> 00:16:39,775
You understand me?

226
00:16:41,892 --> 00:16:44,836
If they still want me,

227
00:16:44,836 --> 00:16:46,934
maybe...

228
00:16:48,265 --> 00:16:53,960
I'll talk to them to postpone the test
until I've sorted things out.

229
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:55,630
Right?

230
00:16:55,630 --> 00:16:57,431
That's my girl.

231
00:17:00,924 --> 00:17:03,622
I mean... like...

232
00:17:03,622 --> 00:17:05,249
"That's my girl!", like...

233
00:17:05,249 --> 00:17:07,297
Your responses have improved a lot.

234
00:17:07,297 --> 00:17:10,062
Like... you know...

235
00:17:10,062 --> 00:17:11,600
Very good.

236
00:17:11,600 --> 00:17:14,168
Good. Yeah.

237
00:17:14,168 --> 00:17:15,551
Cool.

238
00:17:17,113 --> 00:17:19,774
When you can't speak smoothly,
what is it called?

239
00:17:22,044 --> 00:17:24,434
S... s-stutter.

240
00:17:26,855 --> 00:17:28,448
What?

241
00:17:29,470 --> 00:17:30,995
Stutter.

242
00:17:35,268 --> 00:17:37,534
We'll work through it together,
one thing at a time.

243
00:17:38,990 --> 00:17:40,791
I've got your back.

244
00:18:15,372 --> 00:18:17,644
<i>We're now entering the final stretch
of the election campaign,</i>

245
00:18:17,644 --> 00:18:18,714
<i>and right now,</i>

246
00:18:18,714 --> 00:18:21,705
<i>Weechana of the Ruam Thai Chana Party
continues to lead the momentum</i>

247
00:18:21,705 --> 00:18:24,473
<i>as he keeps meeting with voters
across the country.</i>

248
00:18:24,473 --> 00:18:28,172
<i>Weechana also thanked everyone
for their concern and support for Eva,</i>

249
00:18:28,172 --> 00:18:30,702
<i>and said he hopes
she'll be given the time and space to heal.</i>

250
00:18:30,702 --> 00:18:32,924
<i>He added that the party has agreed</i>

251
00:18:32,924 --> 00:18:35,484
<i>not to have Eva return to the campaign trail
for the time being,</i>

252
00:18:35,484 --> 00:18:38,198
<i>out of respect
for the loss she's going through.</i>

253
00:18:38,198 --> 00:18:40,993
Respect her? That's bullshit.

254
00:18:40,993 --> 00:18:43,294
That's complete nonsense.

255
00:18:46,164 --> 00:18:48,134
What is your plan?

256
00:18:49,028 --> 00:18:51,188
I really have broken up with him.

257
00:18:51,188 --> 00:18:53,196
He knows it's over, too.

258
00:18:53,196 --> 00:18:56,206
Right now, I just need to keep a low profile,
gather evidence,

259
00:18:56,206 --> 00:18:58,774
and wait until it's time to take action,
just like the police advised.

260
00:18:59,894 --> 00:19:01,825
You need to be careful.

261
00:19:01,825 --> 00:19:04,833
There's so much injustice in this country

262
00:19:04,833 --> 00:19:07,334
that people have started to see it as normal.

263
00:19:23,641 --> 00:19:26,694
Oh, you're already setting up?

264
00:19:35,311 --> 00:19:36,500
Hey.

265
00:19:36,500 --> 00:19:40,027
You've got a photo shoot from 3 PM
until around 7 tonight,

266
00:19:40,027 --> 00:19:42,489
but you're free before that.

267
00:19:42,489 --> 00:19:44,454
Is there anything special you'd like to do?

268
00:19:45,198 --> 00:19:47,620
I want to go get my stuff from my condo.

269
00:19:47,620 --> 00:19:50,430
I don't want the Chaichana family
to know where I'm staying,

270
00:19:50,430 --> 00:19:52,286
and I'm not going back there again.

271
00:19:52,286 --> 00:19:55,614
As for the gym,
I guess I'll have to find a new one.

272
00:19:55,614 --> 00:19:57,785
As for my new place,

273
00:19:57,785 --> 00:19:59,006
I'll move in with my aunt.

274
00:19:59,006 --> 00:20:00,830
That way, we can look out for each other.

275
00:20:00,830 --> 00:20:03,215
I never asked you to leave.

276
00:20:04,285 --> 00:20:06,081
Wait a second.

277
00:20:06,081 --> 00:20:10,588
Doesn't Weechana already know
where Aunt Da's place is?

278
00:20:10,588 --> 00:20:12,428
Yeah... I know.

279
00:20:12,428 --> 00:20:16,352
But everyone on this street
has known me since I was little.

280
00:20:16,352 --> 00:20:18,164
They practically raised me.

281
00:20:18,164 --> 00:20:22,190
Everyone around here knows me,
so if anything happens,

282
00:20:22,190 --> 00:20:25,111
people will hear it and come help me.

283
00:20:25,111 --> 00:20:27,054
Okay, sure.

284
00:20:27,054 --> 00:20:30,094
Boat and I will stop by regularly
to check on you.

285
00:20:31,182 --> 00:20:34,097
And about the gym,
if you don't mind working out outdoors,

286
00:20:34,097 --> 00:20:36,166
you can use the rooftop of my building.

287
00:20:36,166 --> 00:20:37,967
It's nice and open.

288
00:20:38,614 --> 00:20:40,652
Yeah, that sounds good.

289
00:20:40,652 --> 00:20:43,134
Or you can check it out first.

290
00:20:44,604 --> 00:20:47,329
Then I'd like you to
give me a little more time

291
00:20:47,329 --> 00:20:49,169
for our language lessons.

292
00:20:49,169 --> 00:20:52,108
I want to be fully prepared,
just like we agreed.

293
00:20:52,108 --> 00:20:53,909
You got it.

294
00:21:01,726 --> 00:21:02,905
What's wrong with your eyes?

295
00:21:02,905 --> 00:21:05,094
Nope, it's nothing.

296
00:21:09,748 --> 00:21:11,801
- You can't get in.
- Weechai is my boyfriend.

297
00:21:11,801 --> 00:21:14,857
- You can't get in.
- I told you he is my boyfriend.

298
00:21:14,857 --> 00:21:16,835
Let me go!

299
00:21:20,478 --> 00:21:22,279
It's okay.

300
00:21:24,284 --> 00:21:27,044
Baby. I've been thinking about it.

301
00:21:27,044 --> 00:21:29,652
We could work in L.A.

302
00:21:29,652 --> 00:21:32,974
We've got connections and money.

303
00:21:32,974 --> 00:21:34,894
Pie.

304
00:21:34,894 --> 00:21:36,695
Stop calling my name.

305
00:21:37,454 --> 00:21:41,926
The only thing I'll never do in this world
is to leave you.

306
00:21:41,926 --> 00:21:43,784
And that's a promise.

307
00:21:46,057 --> 00:21:47,982
I love you.

308
00:21:47,982 --> 00:21:50,361
I'll never leave you,

309
00:21:50,361 --> 00:21:53,734
no matter how fucked up your family is.

310
00:21:58,524 --> 00:22:00,374
Do you love me?

311
00:22:01,276 --> 00:22:03,494
If you love me, then that's all that matters.

312
00:22:04,321 --> 00:22:07,334
We can move somewhere quiet,

313
00:22:08,873 --> 00:22:11,034
and I'll cut back on shopping.

314
00:22:12,788 --> 00:22:14,089
Okay?

315
00:22:14,089 --> 00:22:17,174
As long as we're not in anyone's way,

316
00:22:19,308 --> 00:22:21,614
what other people do is their business.

317
00:22:23,404 --> 00:22:25,254
Just the two of us.

318
00:22:37,172 --> 00:22:39,374
So you love me, right?

319
00:22:42,873 --> 00:22:47,143
If it's not you, then who else?

320
00:23:27,044 --> 00:23:29,454
My grandma might be behind Domino's death.

321
00:23:30,350 --> 00:23:31,949
What?

322
00:23:34,356 --> 00:23:37,134
Because she happened to see my brother
with a reporter.

323
00:23:39,785 --> 00:23:42,334
You can't tell a single soul about this.

324
00:23:43,028 --> 00:23:47,268
I told you because I wanted you
to know the whole truth,

325
00:23:47,268 --> 00:23:49,174
so you can think it over again.

326
00:23:50,564 --> 00:23:53,174
I can't bear to lose you the way I lost Mom.

327
00:23:54,553 --> 00:23:57,574
You meant your mom...

328
00:24:00,310 --> 00:24:05,254
Promise me you'll keep this between us...

329
00:24:07,172 --> 00:24:10,234
until I figure out a way
to deal with all of this.

330
00:24:12,126 --> 00:24:14,334
It's for your own safety.

331
00:24:17,556 --> 00:24:19,085
I know.

332
00:24:20,329 --> 00:24:22,854
But my parents aren't just anybody either.

333
00:24:23,529 --> 00:24:26,294
Your grandma isn't
the only scary witch around.

334
00:24:27,130 --> 00:24:29,214
I don't think she'd dare do anything to me.

335
00:24:32,766 --> 00:24:37,070
I'll make sure you never regret choosing me.

336
00:24:37,070 --> 00:24:38,503
Okay?

337
00:25:09,425 --> 00:25:11,226
Are you okay?

338
00:25:12,614 --> 00:25:14,950
Why don't you head back to your aunt's place
and wait there?

339
00:25:14,950 --> 00:25:17,478
I'll have Boat come help me.

340
00:25:17,478 --> 00:25:18,726
It's okay.

341
00:25:18,726 --> 00:25:21,857
It's better if Boat stays with my aunt.

342
00:25:21,857 --> 00:25:25,150
I'll get my clothes,

343
00:25:25,150 --> 00:25:27,646
can you take care of this side?

344
00:25:27,646 --> 00:25:29,132
Sure.

345
00:25:50,286 --> 00:25:51,833
Did you get everything you needed?

346
00:25:51,833 --> 00:25:53,312
Yeah.

347
00:25:57,782 --> 00:25:59,299
Let's go.

348
00:26:33,884 --> 00:26:35,780
Rose.

349
00:26:35,780 --> 00:26:38,204
- Hello.
- Eva, hello.

350
00:26:38,204 --> 00:26:39,454
I'm sorry for your loss.

351
00:26:39,454 --> 00:26:41,012
Thank you.

352
00:26:41,012 --> 00:26:43,406
No, I should be thanking you.
Thank you for coming.

353
00:26:43,406 --> 00:26:44,854
That's what I call true professional spirit.

354
00:26:44,854 --> 00:26:47,985
I don't think I could've done it.

355
00:26:47,985 --> 00:26:50,049
- I will tell...
- Rose, we have a problem.

356
00:26:50,049 --> 00:26:51,323
What is it?

357
00:26:51,323 --> 00:26:52,732
The male model came down with food poisoning.

358
00:26:52,732 --> 00:26:54,460
He's been in the bathroom the whole time.

359
00:26:54,460 --> 00:26:56,124
He's had diarrhea nonstop
and won't come out of the bathroom.

360
00:26:56,124 --> 00:26:57,612
He won't even sit through the briefing
or do any work.

361
00:26:57,612 --> 00:27:00,254
All he wants is to go to the hospital.

362
00:27:00,254 --> 00:27:02,174
What the hell is this?

363
00:27:03,500 --> 00:27:06,886
It's okay.
You should take Eva to get ready first.

364
00:27:06,886 --> 00:27:08,081
- Got it.
- I'll take care of this.

365
00:27:08,081 --> 00:27:09,921
Eva, please follow me.

366
00:27:09,921 --> 00:27:12,044
Rose, this is Pun.

367
00:27:12,044 --> 00:27:13,766
He is my new assistant.

368
00:27:13,766 --> 00:27:14,734
Hello.

369
00:27:14,734 --> 00:27:17,460
He's filling in for Domino
and taking care of me.

370
00:27:17,460 --> 00:27:19,261
Oh, I see.

371
00:27:20,729 --> 00:27:22,430
Please follow me.

372
00:27:22,430 --> 00:27:24,634
- Hold on.
- Yeah?

373
00:27:24,634 --> 00:27:26,210
Hold on one sec.

374
00:27:28,468 --> 00:27:29,860
Hey, Pun.

375
00:27:29,860 --> 00:27:33,254
Would you be interested
in modeling for us today?

376
00:27:34,233 --> 00:27:35,454
We won't be showing much of your face.

377
00:27:35,454 --> 00:27:38,054
This shoot is mainly focused on Eva anyway.

378
00:27:39,796 --> 00:27:42,926
It's your call. I'm not forcing you.

379
00:27:42,926 --> 00:27:44,366
Please, I'm asking you as a favor.

380
00:27:44,366 --> 00:27:48,686
Otherwise,
I'll have to find another male model,

381
00:27:48,686 --> 00:27:51,774
and I'm afraid we won't make Eva's schedule.

382
00:27:55,314 --> 00:27:57,857
Could you please do this for me? For Eva?

383
00:28:02,172 --> 00:28:04,054
I think...

384
00:28:05,180 --> 00:28:07,054
Okay.

385
00:28:07,054 --> 00:28:08,374
Fantastic!

386
00:28:08,374 --> 00:28:10,753
Excellent! Okay.

387
00:28:10,753 --> 00:28:14,400
Alright, you need to take both models
to get ready.

388
00:28:14,400 --> 00:28:16,364
- Thank you so much.
- No problem.

389
00:28:16,364 --> 00:28:18,165
This way, please.

390
00:28:18,965 --> 00:28:20,766
Be careful.

391
00:28:32,125 --> 00:28:33,921
Are you okay?

392
00:28:33,921 --> 00:28:35,722
- Are you okay?
- Okay.

393
00:29:08,726 --> 00:29:12,494
This is so nice! Come on, let's get started.

394
00:29:12,494 --> 00:29:15,034
- Bride, face forward, please.
- Got it.

395
00:29:15,034 --> 00:29:18,094
Groom, turn to the side and wrap your arm
around the bride's waist, please.

396
00:29:20,070 --> 00:29:21,329
Come on.

397
00:29:21,329 --> 00:29:23,913
Just do it. It's okay.

398
00:29:23,913 --> 00:29:25,774
Look at the bride, please.

399
00:29:25,774 --> 00:29:28,515
Look at her.

400
00:29:28,515 --> 00:29:30,974
Give her a loving look.

401
00:29:34,673 --> 00:29:37,014
I think he's still a little stiff.

402
00:29:39,057 --> 00:29:40,641
Show her a little more love.

403
00:29:40,641 --> 00:29:45,174
Show me what's in your heart.
You're getting married today.

404
00:29:48,353 --> 00:29:50,651
Yes! That's it! Now you're in love.
Stay right there!

405
00:29:50,651 --> 00:29:53,233
Alright, let's switch poses.

406
00:29:53,233 --> 00:29:54,958
Okay, let's do this instead.

407
00:29:54,958 --> 00:29:56,217
Put your arms around each other.

408
00:29:56,217 --> 00:29:58,094
Eva, wrap your arms around his neck.

409
00:29:58,094 --> 00:30:00,254
And Pun...

410
00:30:00,254 --> 00:30:01,945
- wrap your arms around her waist.
- Wrap my arms?

411
00:30:01,945 --> 00:30:04,068
And look at each other.

412
00:30:10,924 --> 00:30:12,972
Pun, your nose.

413
00:30:12,972 --> 00:30:16,054
Touch her cheek with your nose.
Eva, is it okay?

414
00:30:16,721 --> 00:30:18,668
- Yeah, let's do this.
- Okay.

415
00:30:18,668 --> 00:30:20,974
Touch her cheek with your nose.

416
00:30:26,670 --> 00:30:28,471
Damn it!

417
00:30:35,548 --> 00:30:37,349
Goddamn it.

418
00:30:49,315 --> 00:30:50,649
Hey.

419
00:30:50,649 --> 00:30:52,054
Get Eva's schedule.

420
00:30:52,054 --> 00:30:54,670
Find out where Eva will be tomorrow

421
00:30:54,670 --> 00:30:56,471
and what she'll be doing.

422
00:30:57,281 --> 00:30:59,841
What the fuck are you waiting for? Go!

423
00:30:59,841 --> 00:31:01,486
Yes, sir.

424
00:31:22,233 --> 00:31:23,999
Hello.

425
00:31:26,633 --> 00:31:28,990
- Hello, Eva.
- Hello.

426
00:31:28,990 --> 00:31:31,668
Hi, I'm Pun, Eva's assistant.
We spoke on the phone.

427
00:31:31,668 --> 00:31:34,720
This way, please.
I'll take you to the dressing room first.

428
00:31:34,720 --> 00:31:36,101
- Okay.
- Sure.

429
00:31:41,993 --> 00:31:43,895
As you probably already know,

430
00:31:43,895 --> 00:31:48,294
today's event is to introduce
our new brand ambassador, who is you.

431
00:31:48,294 --> 00:31:51,180
The host will kick things off
with the opening remarks,

432
00:31:51,180 --> 00:31:53,782
then we'll officially introduce you.

433
00:31:53,782 --> 00:31:57,374
We also have a little surprise
prepared for you.

434
00:31:58,145 --> 00:32:00,625
A surprise? You shouldn't have.

435
00:32:00,625 --> 00:32:02,006
Not at all. It's our pleasure.

436
00:32:02,006 --> 00:32:06,097
We're all so happy
to be working with you, Eva.

437
00:32:06,097 --> 00:32:08,036
Please make yourself comfortable
in this room for now.

438
00:32:08,036 --> 00:32:11,374
If there's anything you need,
don't hesitate to let our staff know.

439
00:32:11,374 --> 00:32:14,510
We'll come get you
when it's time for standby.

440
00:32:14,510 --> 00:32:15,744
- Thank you.
- No problem.

441
00:32:15,744 --> 00:32:17,175
This way.

442
00:32:27,841 --> 00:32:28,966
Here.

443
00:32:28,966 --> 00:32:32,289
Have some protein so you'll have the energy,

444
00:32:32,289 --> 00:32:34,254
and so you don't lose muscle.

445
00:32:35,745 --> 00:32:37,990
- Hey.
- What?

446
00:32:38,746 --> 00:32:41,862
Do you think we should have someone
stay with my aunt?

447
00:32:41,862 --> 00:32:43,663
I'm worried about her.

448
00:32:44,863 --> 00:32:46,664
I can go be with her.

449
00:32:48,185 --> 00:32:50,134
Are you that worried about her?

450
00:32:54,404 --> 00:32:57,966
Actually,
the reason I brought Boat with us...

451
00:32:57,966 --> 00:32:59,972
is because people could come at us
from anywhere.

452
00:32:59,972 --> 00:33:02,614
I figured it'd be better
if there were two of us.

453
00:33:03,337 --> 00:33:06,644
And we also asked the neighbor
to stay with your aunt.

454
00:33:06,644 --> 00:33:08,308
I think she'll be fine.

455
00:33:08,308 --> 00:33:10,109
It's broad daylight.

456
00:33:12,052 --> 00:33:13,853
You're right.

457
00:33:15,588 --> 00:33:17,865
Try to relax.

458
00:33:17,865 --> 00:33:19,934
You'll get to go see your aunt soon.

459
00:33:21,331 --> 00:33:23,956
Come on. Drink it.

460
00:33:24,964 --> 00:33:26,667
It's delicious.

461
00:33:27,414 --> 00:33:29,004
It's good stuff.

462
00:33:29,004 --> 00:33:30,814
People who lift know.

463
00:33:33,926 --> 00:33:35,436
How does it taste?

464
00:33:35,436 --> 00:33:37,534
It's good, right?

465
00:33:38,150 --> 00:33:42,694
Let's give a big round of applause
for Eva Yanin!

466
00:33:52,516 --> 00:33:56,317
Hello, please have a seat.

467
00:33:58,174 --> 00:34:01,454
Wow! You're so gorgeous.

468
00:34:01,454 --> 00:34:04,892
How does it feel to officially
be part of our family?

469
00:34:04,892 --> 00:34:08,913
I'm truly honored and very happy

470
00:34:08,913 --> 00:34:13,694
to officially become
part of the Eterno family.

471
00:34:29,193 --> 00:34:33,236
And now we've reached
the final part of today's event.

472
00:34:33,236 --> 00:34:37,225
But this might just be
the most important moment of the day for you.

473
00:34:37,225 --> 00:34:40,574
We have a special surprise for you.

474
00:34:45,246 --> 00:34:51,254
We're truly honored
to be part of such a special moment.

475
00:34:54,254 --> 00:34:55,856
What is that?

476
00:35:09,340 --> 00:35:11,334
Wow, that's a huge bouquet!

477
00:35:25,777 --> 00:35:28,014
Hello.

478
00:35:28,014 --> 00:35:29,815
Thank you.

479
00:35:35,449 --> 00:35:37,334
Will you excuse me?

480
00:35:41,750 --> 00:35:43,417
Look at the camera.

481
00:35:54,062 --> 00:35:58,351
You know what your answer should be,
don't you?

482
00:36:41,969 --> 00:36:43,377
Will you marry me?

483
00:36:43,377 --> 00:36:46,236
Say yes! Say yes!

484
00:36:46,236 --> 00:36:49,294
Marry him! Marry him!

485
00:36:49,294 --> 00:36:51,534
Say yes! Say yes!
